  "conclusion": "Given the reviewed genuine writer/guard chain, two distinct completed Local receipt inserts cannot successfully seal the same bundle/revision: requests/generations have distinct identities, canonical source origin binds the unique request identity, and common PK rejects differing canonical requests for samebundle/revision even if UUID generation collides. All Local producers use revision1. Same-request replay returns its existing receipt. The JSON lookup is not independently schema-unique or STRICT; unrelated corrupted/owner-authored data could violate its assumption, but no such authorised write path was found. This is not installed-data proof.",
